    "body": "From the user (2026-11-11): the plate maker publishes **simplified STEP models** of its plates and mod vises. Plan:\n- **Grid from an imported plate:** besides the generic parametric plate, let #819 derive the grid from an IMPORTED plate's holes, using the existing hole detection (the detect-holes rule behind MCP `detect_holes`). Snapping to \"hole C3\" then works on a user's real plate, not only on the built-in generic one.\n- **Test input:** the user's own downloaded plate STEP is the local test input. It's never committed or shipped, and the generic built-in geometry isn't derived from it (Clean-Room Protocol; vendor terms).",
